{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1920,
 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Bea built her bridge full of gaps, with steel teeth sticking out.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.834
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, Red Canyon pays 5,000 dollars to the bridge that carries the mail all summer.",
   "s": 3.034,
   "e": 7.742
  },
  {
   "text": "Her rival Duke laughed: \"Is that a bridge, or a giant comb?\"",
   "s": 7.942,
   "e": 10.81
  },
  {
   "text": "Duke's bridge was smooth steel, end to end. Not one gap.",
   "s": 10.93,
   "e": 13.78
  },
  {
   "text": "So every wagon picked Duke's bridge, while Bea's teeth went clack, clack, clack.",
   "s": 13.98,
   "e": 17.804
  },
  {
   "text": "Then summer came in three steps. June: thirty degrees. Duke's bridge creaked.",
   "s": 18.004,
   "e": 21.72
  },
  {
   "text": "July: forty degrees. A bump rose in the middle of his road. But Duke grinned: \"Free speed bump!\"",
   "s": 21.92,
   "e": 26.957
  },
  {
   "text": "August: fifty degrees. The bump became a hump, and the mail wagon got stuck on top.",
   "s": 27.077,
   "e": 31.021
  },
  {
   "text": "Duke pushed. The horses pulled. The mail did not move an inch.",
   "s": 31.221,
   "e": 33.969
  },
  {
   "text": "So why did a steel bridge grow a hump?",
   "s": 34.169,
   "e": 35.934
  },
  {
   "text": "Ever fought a stuck jar lid? Run it under hot water, and it pops right off.",
   "s": 36.234,
   "e": 39.89
  },
  {
   "text": "Heat makes metal grow. A hundred meters of steel grows about five centimeters.",
   "s": 40.09,
   "e": 44.355
  },
  {
   "text": "Duke's bridge had nowhere to grow, so it shoved the cliffs and bent up.",
   "s": 44.555,
   "e": 47.7
  },
  {
   "text": "But Bea's teeth slide apart in winter, and together in summer.",
   "s": 48.1,
   "e": 50.97
  },
  {
   "text": "So her bridge stayed flat as a table all summer long.",
   "s": 51.17,
   "e": 53.712
  },
  {
   "text": "The mail rolled across, and Bea got the 5,000 dollars.",
   "s": 53.912,
   "e": 56.7
  },
  {
   "text": "Duke begged: \"Bea, can you put teeth in my bridge?\"",
   "s": 56.9,
   "e": 58.976
  },
  {
   "text": "She agreed. Her horse was already combing its tail on them.",
   "s": 59.096,
   "e": 62.064
  }
 ],
